{title: Jesus Paid It All}
{artist: Elvina M. Hall / John T. Grape}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [D]hear the Saviour say
"Thy [G]strength indeed is [D]small
Child of [D]weakness, watch and [A7]pray
Find in [D]Me thine all in all"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Jesus paid it [G]all
[D]All to Him I [A7]owe
[D]Sin had left a [G]crimson stain
He [D]washed it [A7]white as [D]snow
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Lord, now in[D]deed I find
Thy [G]power, and Thine a[D]lone
Can change the [D]leper's spots
And [A7]melt the heart of [D]stone
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
For [D]nothing good have I
Where[G]by Thy grace to [D]claim
I'll wash my [D]garments white
In the [A7]blood of Calvary's [D]Lamb
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
And [D]when before the throne
I [G]stand in Him com[D]plete
"Jesus [D]died my soul to save"
My [A7]lips shall still re[D]peat
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
